                <invention-title lang="de">VERFAHREN ZUR ERHÖHUNG DER EMPFINDLICHKEIT VON RFID-ETIKETTEN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROCÉDÉ POUR AUGMENTER LA SENSIBILITÉ D'UNE ÉTIQUETTE RFID</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">METHOD TO INCREASE RFID TAG SENSITIVITY</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A radio-frequency identification (RFID) tag, comprising: a main antenna configured to receive RF signal and wirelessly harvests power from the received RF signal; a first impedance coupled to the main antenna, wherein the first impedance is deterministic of a reflection coefficient of the main antenna; and a switching circuit communicatively coupled to the main antenna and a second impedance, wherein the switching circuit is configured to couple the second impedance with the main antenna to modify the reflection coefficient of the main antenna, wherein the switching circuit is configured to operate the main antenna in a low reflectance period and a high reflectance period, wherein during the low reflectance period, the main antenna is disconnected from the second impedance and the main antenna is configured to harvest power from the received RF signal, and wherein during the high reflectance period, the main antenna is connected to the second impedance and the main antenna is configured to reflect the RF signal, without shorting the main antenna, while continuing to harvest power from the received RF signal.</p>
            </abstract>
